  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be the plane passing through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math>, if the distance of the points<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> respectively, then the positive value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
